# Code Review Guidelines
Rule Type: Always

## Review Requirements
### Required Reviews
- Peer review for all trading logic
- Security review for all IBKR interactions
- Performance review for realtime operations
- Strategy logic review
- Error handling review

### Review Checklist
- Error handling
- Logging
- Documentation
- Test coverage
- Security
- Performance

## Review Process
### Pre-Review
- Self-review code
- Run tests
- Update documentation
- Check formatting
- Verify requirements

### Review Steps
1. Code quality review
2. Functionality review
3. Security review
4. Performance review
5. Documentation review

## Review Focus
### Trading Logic
- Signal generation
- Entry/exit logic
- Risk management
- Position sizing
- Error handling

### System Logic
- Connection management
- Data processing
- Order management
- Error recovery
- Performance optimization

## Review Criteria
### Code Quality
- Code organization
- Naming conventions
- Documentation
- Error handling
- Logging

### Functionality
- Business logic
- Trading rules
- Risk management
- Performance
- Security

## Documentation
### Review Documentation
- Code comments
- Function documentation
- Class documentation
- Usage examples
- Change documentation

### Review Process
- Document review comments
- Track review status
- Update documentation
- Maintain review history
- Follow up on changes

## Testing
### Review Tests
- Unit tests
- Integration tests
- Performance tests
- Security tests
- Edge cases

### Test Coverage
- Code coverage
- Critical paths
- Error conditions
- Performance scenarios
- Security scenarios

## Security
### Security Review
- Input validation
- Error handling
- Access control
- Data protection
- Secure coding

### Compliance
- Trading regulations
- Security standards
- Best practices
- Documentation
- Audit trails

## Performance
### Performance Review
- Algorithm efficiency
- Resource usage
- Response times
- Scalability
- Optimization

### Monitoring
- Performance metrics
- Resource usage
- Error rates
- Success rates
- System health

## Follow-up
### Post-Review
- Address comments
- Update code
- Update tests
- Update documentation
- Verify changes

### Verification
- Run tests
- Check performance
- Verify security
- Update documentation
- Final review
